        "original_id": "df0fade8-e443-58cf-8843-a2c95b795fb5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Old German Shepherd Dog, Black Mouth Cur\n- Organizations: Fédération Cynologique Internationale\n- Places: Southern United States\n- Concepts: long-haired variation, separate breed recognition\n\nFacts:\n- The Old German Shepherd Dog is a controversial name for the long-haired variation of the German Shepherd Dog.\n- The long-haired variation of the German Shepherd Dog is called Langstockhaariger Deutscher Schäferhund in German.\n- The Fédération Cynologique Internationale does not recognize the Old German Shepherd Dog as a separate breed.\n- The Black Mouth Cur is a hunting and cattle dog.\n- The Black Mouth Cur originated in the Southern United States.",
